      {
        "id": 195347,
        "name": "Phantom5613",
        "username": "Phantom5613",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/{size}/1906_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-05-07T18:48:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm surprised that no one has said anything about the recent GTG newsletter that revealed the release of the Sentinels Comics RPG Starter Kit.</p><p>They talk about how the kit will be comprised of a sum total of thirteen booklets, the first being a 'how to play/how to run an adventure' guide for both players and GMs.</p><p>The next six booklets are pre-made character folios for the Freedom Five and Unity, and will give you all the info you need to learn how to play that character and how the character sheet info is relevant to the game.</p><p>The&nbsp;last six books will be episodic game adventures with an over-arching plot, picking up right in the middle of the aftermath of the SotM card game. Each will act as a complete issue of a comic book, each one introducing useful game mechanics.</p><p>The Sentinels Comics RPG Starter Kit will be for sale August 2017 for $19.95.</p>",
