      {
        "id": 195353,
        "name": "The Burning Stickman",
        "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-07-19T19:21:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Ehkrickor\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ehkrickor/48/2035_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ehkrickor:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think that even if OblivAeon shiped around GenCon delaying the RPG kickstarter till after christmas is a good idea, cause then &gt;G's target audience will have more disposable income. I know i will,</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, that was largely the issue with the Season 2 videogame kickstarter – it came right on the heals of OblivAeon's kickstarter, where many people had already spent a large sum of money, and was asking largely the same audience for even more.</p>",
